[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  ⚡  Ubuntu → ZFS\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;36m[1. Scan disk + choose method]\u001b[0m | 2. Prepare disk | 3. Convert ext4 to ZFS | 4. Finish disk + boot setup\r\n  5. Snapshots + recovery + growth\r\n\r\n  Scan the selected data disk and its mount settings\r\n\r\nMake a full offsite backup before proceeding. Conversion can destroy data.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\rzfsify  /  SETUP\u001b[K\r\n\r\u001b[K\r\n\r\u001b[1;36mHow would you like to move to ZFS?\u001b[0m                                        \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mYOUR DISK  /  PLAN PREVIEW\u001b[0m\u001b[K\r\n\r                                                                          \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0m/dev/vdc\u001b[K\r\n\r\u001b[1;36m› 1  Keep everything · 50/50 [recommended]\u001b[0m                                \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0m805.3 MB used / 8.4 GB FS\u001b[K\r\n\r     \u001b[90mNeeds room for two copies. The original stays until verification.\u001b[0m    \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0m\u001b[K\r\n\r                                                                          \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0m  \u001b[33m███\u001b[0m\u001b[90m░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░\u001b[0m\u001b[K\r\n\r\u001b[1m  2  Keep everything · slice-by-slice\u001b[0m                                     \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0mCurrent filesystem usage · shaded = free\u001b[K\r\n\r     \u001b[90munavailable for data volumes.\u001b[0m                                        \u001b[90m │ \u001b[0m\u001b[K\r\n\r                                                 "]
